  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "METL5bGVpWTOZZc6bliZNvOe17YhEJluSEEspZ8S7dx/31vL+f/yzn/9Yh6R/sea7ElsQXNC59QwclirUNKUxw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 19386464,
  "published": "2026-10-13T20:41:40.043Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Changed\n\n- *Breaking*: [Update FSharp.Compiler.Service to 43.12.402 and FSharp.Core to 10.1.402](https://github.com/ionide/FSharp.Analyzers.SDK/pull/346). FSharp.Compiler.Service is not binary compatible between releases, so analyzers built against 0.39 need to be rebuilt.\n- FSharp.Compiler.Service is now pinned to an exact version, like FSharp.Core already was. NuGet now warns (NU1608) when an analyzer project resolves a newer FSharp.Compiler.Service than the SDK was built with, instead of accepting it silently.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- `InlineAnnotation` is `AlwaysInline` again for `inline` values from assemblies built with F# 4.7 or older ([dotnet/fsharp#20260](https://github.com/dotnet/fsharp/pull/20260)).\n- An analyzer assembly with a dependency that cannot be loaded, such as a newer FSharp.Compiler.Service than the tool ships, is now skipped with an error. Previously the `FileNotFoundException` crashed the run and no analyzer ran at all.",
  "repository": {
